  "notes": "Sehwi orthography is similar to Akan. Acute accents mark high tone, while tildes mark nasalised vowels. Digraphs like 'ky', 'dw', 'ny', 'nw', and 'ng' represent palatalised, labialised, or velar consonants. The exact phonetic realization of 'dw' and 'ky' is mapped conservatively to alveolo-palatal affricates. Nasalisation is handled by the combining tilde in \"diacritics\"; precomposed nasal vowels are therefore not listed as separate graphemes.",
